<%# locals: slots - CollectionStats::SetCards rows at unit 'printing', labels, pagy %>
<%#
  The set as a checklist. One tile per SLOT - a printing in a finish - so the regular Ancestral
  Katana and the foil Ancestral Katana are two tiles, because they are two cards to go and find.
  NEO is 514 printings and just over a thousand slots.

  The same art appears twice, which is the honest answer rather than a shortcut: Scryfall has one
  scan per printing and a foil is that same picture. What separates the two tiles is the chip, the
  price and whether it is greyed.

  Tiles are per printing, not per card, for the same reason - Jin-Gitaxias is seven printings in NEO
  and the borderless one is a different object to want than the soft-glow showcase one. The table is
  where a card is a card; here a card is a picture.

  Deliberately not clickable. In the table a row opens onto its printings and its price history;
  here the hover preview is the whole interaction, and a grid where every tile expands something
  underneath it stops being a grid.
%>

<div class="mb-24">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 xl:grid-cols-6">
    <% slots.each do |slot| %>
      <% label = labels[slot[:id]]&.join(" ")&.presence || (slot[:in_base] ? "base run" : "variant") %>

      <div
        class="
          relative overflow-hidden transition-transform rounded-xl
          hover:scale-105
        "
        data-controller="card-hover"
        data-card-hover-image-value="<%= slot[:image_large] %>"
        data-card-hover-name-value="<%= slot[:name] %>"
        data-action="mouseenter->card-hover#show mouseleave->card-hover#hide mousemove->card-hover#move"
      >
        <% if slot[:image].present? %>
          <%= image_tag slot[:image],
            alt: "#{slot[:name]} - #{label} #{slot[:finish]}",
            loading: "lazy",
            class: "w-full rounded-xl shadow-lg #{"grayscale opacity-40" unless slot[:owned]}" %>
        <% else %>
          <div
            class="
              flex items-center justify-center w-full p-2 text-sm text-center
              rounded-xl bg-background text-grey-text aspect-5/7
            "
          >
            <%= slot[:name] %>
          </div>
        <% end %>

        <span
          class="
            absolute px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs rounded top-1 left-1 bg-black/70
            text-grey-text
          "
        >
          #<%= slot[:number] %>
        </span>

        <span class="absolute px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs rounded top-1 right-1 <%= slot[:owned] ? "bg-accent-50 text-badge-text" : "bg-black/70 text-grey-text" %>">
          <%= slot[:owned] ? "x#{slot[:copies]}" : "missing" %>
        </span>

        <div
          class="
            absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 px-2 py-2 text-xs rounded-b-xl
            bg-black/80
          "
        >
          <div class="font-medium truncate text-nine-white">
            <%= slot[:name].to_s.split("//").first %>
          </div>

          <div class="truncate text-grey-text/60" title="<%= label %>">
            <%= label %>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-1 mt-1">
            <span class="px-1 border rounded shrink-0 <%= finish_chip_class(slot[:finish]) %>">
              <%= slot[:finish] %>
            </span>

            <span class="text-grey-text">
              <%= number_to_currency(slot[:price]) %>
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% if pagy %>
    <div
      class="
        flex flex-col items-center justify-between w-full gap-2 p-6 mt-4
        text-sm md:flex-row
      "
    >
      <%== pagy.info_tag() %>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto"><%== pagy.series_nav() %></div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
